1
00:00:07,132 --> 00:00:10,093
[crowd cheering and applauding]

2
00:00:10,176 --> 00:00:13,972
["Too Much" by Dove Cameron playing]

3
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:17,225
<i>I'm Teagan Tao.</i>

4
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:22,897
<i>Those are my parents.</i>

5
00:00:22,981 --> 00:00:26,234
<i>My dad owns boutique hotels, loves rowing.</i>

6
00:00:26,317 --> 00:00:30,739
Remember, stay within your pace,
keep it steady. You got this!

7
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:31,740
[Teagan] <i>And my mom…</i>

8
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:34,117
-Go, Teagan, whoo!
-[Teagan] <i>…tries.</i>

9
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,495
-Wow, it's really packed here.
-It's okay, I'm manifesting a spot.

10
00:00:37,579 --> 00:00:38,747
-Of course you are.
-Look!

11
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:42,167
[Teagan] <i>They're still madly in love.</i>
<i>It's gross.</i>

12
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:45,170
<i>To be a rower is to be all in.</i>

13
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:49,299
<i>Every 6 a.m. practice,</i>
<i>every punishing workout leads to this.</i>

14
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:50,967
[horn blows]

15
00:00:51,051 --> 00:00:54,179
<i>♪ If you say I'm too much</i>
<i>Baby, go find less ♪</i>

16
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:56,931
-Go, Teagan!
-Yes!

17
00:00:57,682 --> 00:01:01,311
<i>♪ If I'm such a big deal</i>
<i>Maybe you're too little ♪</i>

18
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:04,481
<i>♪ Ooh, ooh, it's tough</i>
<i>I'm too, too, too much ♪</i>

19
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:05,732
Come on, Teag!

20
00:01:05,815 --> 00:01:08,777
<i>♪ Baby, I ain't under pressure ♪</i>

21
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:12,530
<i>♪ Oh, oh, gather up, return to sender ♪</i>

22
00:01:12,614 --> 00:01:16,242
<i>♪ Oh, oh, baby, I ain't under pressure ♪</i>

23
00:01:16,326 --> 00:01:18,411
[phone buzzing]

24
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:23,291
I have to take this.

25
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:25,085
-What?
-It's work.

26
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:27,462
Okay. Go, Teagan!

27
00:01:27,545 --> 00:01:29,798
Hey. Hey.

28
00:01:29,881 --> 00:01:30,965
I love you.

29
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:35,428
Okay. Oh, my…! Oh, my God, Teagan!

30
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:38,890
<i>♪ …can't keep up, stay below, I guess ♪</i>

31
00:01:38,973 --> 00:01:42,310
<i>♪ If I'm such a big deal</i>
<i>Maybe you're too little ♪</i>

32
00:01:42,393 --> 00:01:45,021
[Ella] Oh, my God, go, Teagan!

33
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:48,149
[Teagan] <i>Your muscles are screaming,</i>
<i>but you push harder.</i>

34
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:50,527
-Come on.
<i>-You fight to get a split second ahead.</i>

35
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:53,154
[Ella] Teagan! Whoo!

36
00:01:53,238 --> 00:01:56,616
-[screaming]
-Yes, Teagan, yes! Oh, my God!

37
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,577
[announcer] <i>The winner is Teagan Tao.</i>

38
00:01:59,661 --> 00:02:00,829
[phone dinging]

39
00:02:03,039 --> 00:02:05,041
[sirens approaching]

40
00:02:05,708 --> 00:02:07,252
[Ella] You did it!

41
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:08,169
[laughing]

42
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:09,295
[crowd clamoring]

43
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:11,673
[ominous music playing]

44
00:02:11,756 --> 00:02:13,758
[Teagan] <i>And when you finally get it…</i>

45
00:02:14,884 --> 00:02:16,886
Mrs. Tao, can you come with us?

46
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,805
Uh, don't touch me, please.

47
00:02:18,888 --> 00:02:20,640
[agent] We have questions
about your husband.

48
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:25,645
<i>[Teagan] …someone else's split-second</i>
<i>decision takes everything away.</i>

49
00:02:25,728 --> 00:02:28,022
[emotional music playing]

50
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:31,568
<i>Turns out, my dad had</i>
<i>defrauded investors out of millions.</i>

51
00:02:31,651 --> 00:02:32,861
I need to see a warrant.

52
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:35,530
[Teagan] <i>He disappeared</i>
<i>with my friends' parents' money,</i>

53
00:02:35,613 --> 00:02:38,825
<i>while my mom and I were left with the FBI.</i>

54
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:41,035
-[school bell ringing]
-Hey.

55
00:02:41,119 --> 00:02:43,079
<i>I lost all my friends.</i>

56
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:45,331
<i>They took all our money,</i>

57
00:02:45,415 --> 00:02:49,002
<i>except for the education trust</i>
<i>that my dad set up.</i>

58
00:02:54,382 --> 00:02:58,803
<i>My mom and I had to leave LA</i>
<i>and head back to her hometown.</i>

59
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:03,850
<i>My life as I knew it was over.</i>

60
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:09,647
<i>But little did I know,</i>
<i>my new life was just beginning.</i>

61
00:03:10,148 --> 00:03:16,237
["Triple Seven" by Wishy playing]

62
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:26,497
<i>♪ A little bit uncertain</i>
<i>I wasn't really sure ♪</i>

63
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:28,499
Eagle's Cove.

64
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,169
Is this where Dad's hiding out?

65
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:32,337
That's not funny.

66
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,881
Neither is ghosting your family
for six months.

67
00:03:34,964 --> 00:03:39,469
Yeah, well, he's still your dad.
And we don't know the whole story, so…

68
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:41,346
[Teagan] Ah, yes. Denial.

69
00:03:41,429 --> 00:03:43,890
The most annoying
of the coping strategies.

70
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:47,435
[Ella] It's not denial.
It's positivity. And it could be worse.

71
00:03:47,518 --> 00:03:48,478
[Teagan] What's worse?

72
00:03:48,561 --> 00:03:51,356
[Ella] I could be drowning you
with love and attention.

73
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:53,524
[Teagan] You're right. That is worse.

74
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:54,567
[laughing]

75
00:03:55,735 --> 00:03:58,279
Are there any people here,
or is it all just…

76
00:03:58,363 --> 00:04:00,031
-trees?
-[crow cawing]

77
00:04:00,114 --> 00:04:02,242
Oh! There's the fudge store!

78
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:04,285
You don't like fudge.

79
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:09,207
No. Nobody actually likes fudge,
but I like that it exists.

80
00:04:09,791 --> 00:04:12,543
Here's the Crab Shack.
I used to work there, you know.

81
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:14,754
They make the best crab cakes.

82
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:17,799
That's a heinous understanding
of what a cake is.

83
00:04:17,882 --> 00:04:18,716
[Ella chuckles]

84
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:21,469
Does this new school
even have a rowing team?

85
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:22,887
Yeah. It's on their website.

86
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:24,222
They must suck,

87
00:04:24,305 --> 00:04:27,558
because I don't see them
on any of the top ten rankings.

88
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:31,271
Easton Prep is at the top
of all the academic lists.

89
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:36,234
Do you remember Nanny and Grandpa's
from when you were younger?

90
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:38,778
[Teagan] From when I was four? Not really.

91
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,738
[Ella] You're gonna love it.

92
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:45,868
Hm.

93
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:48,204
[Ella] Here we are.

94
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:50,581
I always wanted to perform an exorcism.

95
00:04:50,665 --> 00:04:54,168
Okay, yeah,
maybe it could use a little sprucing up.

96
00:04:56,546 --> 00:04:59,424
-Is this, uh, Nana's stuff?
-[soft music playing]

97
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:04,679
[Ella] Yeah. I didn't have a chance
to pack everything up after the funeral.

98
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:06,889
[door closes]

99
00:05:10,852 --> 00:05:13,521
[Teagan] No wonder they used to visit us.

100
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:17,400
Welcome home!

101
00:05:20,069 --> 00:05:23,823
So it's not exactly like our old place,

102
00:05:23,906 --> 00:05:27,618
but, uh, I think
we can really make a go of it.

103
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:29,454
This house might be growing fur.

104
00:05:29,537 --> 00:05:34,167
Or it just… needs new curtains.

105
00:05:35,835 --> 00:05:38,129
Okay, do you really wanna be here?

106
00:05:38,212 --> 00:05:41,591
I mean, you love California as much as me.
We are in the middle of nowhere.

107
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:43,426
Oh come on, it's not that bad.

108
00:05:43,509 --> 00:05:45,887
I mean, we're only
a half hour from Starbucks.

109
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:48,181
Mom, the coaches from Stanford
were scouting me.

110
00:05:48,264 --> 00:05:51,309
I'm on a D1 scholarship track.
How are they gonna see me out here?

111
00:05:51,392 --> 00:05:53,895
I know you're worried, okay?

112
00:05:53,978 --> 00:05:57,398
-I know. But it's gonna be okay.
-How?

113
00:05:57,899 --> 00:05:59,067
[sighs]

114
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:00,151
I'm gonna get some air.

115
00:06:00,234 --> 00:06:04,072
I'll be back in an hour
if this… house stays up until then.

116
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:05,573
[Ella groans quietly]

117
00:06:08,201 --> 00:06:09,535
[door closes]

118
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:15,041
["Care" by Hana Vu playing]

119
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:18,211
<i>♪ I'm waking up to the sun ♪</i>

120
00:06:18,294 --> 00:06:23,966
<i>♪ And I find it all too much ♪</i>

121
00:06:27,136 --> 00:06:30,556
<i>♪ Oh, call this dawn, don't you know ♪</i>

122
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:35,061
<i>♪ I can't even talk about you ♪</i>

123
00:06:38,147 --> 00:06:40,566
<i>♪ And I… ♪</i>

124
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:41,526
[screams]

125
00:06:43,653 --> 00:06:47,240
[Teagan] Hey!
Watch where you're going! What the…

126
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:51,786
-You're not gonna ask if I'm okay?
-You seem okay.

127
00:06:51,869 --> 00:06:53,788
Are you going to apologize for hitting me?

128
00:06:53,871 --> 00:06:56,416
You're zooming down the sidewalk,
okay? That's on you.

129
00:06:59,627 --> 00:07:01,671
Your chain slipped.
Do you know how to fix it?

130
00:07:03,256 --> 00:07:04,257
-Okay.
-Uh…

131
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:16,352
-What are you, um…
-Fixing your chain.

132
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:24,152
So do you live here?

133
00:07:24,735 --> 00:07:25,945
Yes.

134
00:07:27,029 --> 00:07:29,365
What do you do for fun?

135
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:35,163
We have clambakes, tubing, fudge.
If that's your thing.

136
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:37,915
All right, come here. See the drivetrain?

137
00:07:37,999 --> 00:07:40,877
You gotta clean it
or your chain is just gonna keep slipping.

138
00:07:42,962 --> 00:07:44,172
This thing?

139
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:48,926
This one…

140
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:50,803
should do it.

141
00:07:54,932 --> 00:07:57,602
You didn't have to do that, but, uh…

142
00:07:58,769 --> 00:08:00,062
thanks.

143
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:02,940
I'm Teagan. I just moved here.

144
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:05,109
Cam. Dillinger.

145
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:08,946
["Gospel" by Jean Dawson playing]

146
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:10,948
Okay, look, I gotta go.

147
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:14,243
Learn to fix your bike, okay?
Next time, I won't be around.

148
00:08:15,119 --> 00:08:18,289
<i>♪ Fall in love with a New York model ♪</i>

149
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:25,546
<i>♪ Take some drugs outside of Chicago ♪</i>

150
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:27,089
You hit me!

151
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:28,883
[song ends]

152
00:08:28,966 --> 00:08:30,676
<i>There are four parts to a stroke.</i>

153
00:08:31,802 --> 00:08:35,890
<i>The catch, the drive,</i>
<i>the finish, and the recovery.</i>

154
00:08:35,973 --> 00:08:40,603
<i>Rowing, like life,</i>
<i>is a constant state of resetting yourself.</i>

155
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:42,730
<i>The most important part is the catch,</i>

156
00:08:42,813 --> 00:08:45,149
<i>where your blade grabs the water.</i>
<i>It's what anchors you.</i>

157
00:08:45,233 --> 00:08:50,321
<i>A bad catch can kill your run,</i>
<i>but a good catch will send you soaring.</i>

158
00:08:50,404 --> 00:08:51,322
[screams]

159
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:55,284
Okay, is this too much tweed
or not enough?

160
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:59,080
Button up and tuck the collar.
There's a little too much clavicle.

161
00:08:59,163 --> 00:09:02,208
I never thought about my clavicle. Hey!

162
00:09:02,291 --> 00:09:03,709
Why are you all dressed up?

163
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:07,797
I have a job interview.
This is the one, I can feel it.

164
00:09:10,132 --> 00:09:13,469
[Teagan] Whoa. Can a building
have a British accent?

165
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:15,012
[Ella] I love the campus.

166
00:09:15,096 --> 00:09:18,766
I always wanted to go here.
Not that they were admitting girls then.

167
00:09:19,642 --> 00:09:21,811
[sighs] You're gonna love it.

168
00:09:24,564 --> 00:09:25,565
[Teagan] Okay.

169
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:32,029
[Ella] Make friends.

170
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:34,407
Okay.

171
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:38,119
[Ella clears throat]

172
00:09:38,786 --> 00:09:40,580
-Bye.
-Bye.

173
00:09:42,915 --> 00:09:44,375
"Make friends"?

174
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:52,633
[elegant string music playing]

175
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:54,010
[Teagan] Okay.

176
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:57,054
[girl laughs] This happens every time.

177
00:09:57,138 --> 00:09:58,472
[girls 2] It's so funny.

178
00:09:58,556 --> 00:09:59,682
Where is she going?

179
00:09:59,765 --> 00:10:03,436
[girl] Round and round and round and…

180
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:05,646
Hi! New girl!

181
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:08,608
Wow. What's your name?

182
00:10:08,691 --> 00:10:10,610
I'm Teagan Tao.

183
00:10:10,693 --> 00:10:13,988
Britney Garner. Student council president.

184
00:10:14,071 --> 00:10:17,783
Yeah, I know what you must be thinking.
Garner, like Senator Garner.

185
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:20,578
Well, that's right.
Like mother, like daughter.

186
00:10:20,661 --> 00:10:22,663
Vote for Garner 2044. [giggles]

187
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:24,999
I'll put that in my calendar.

188
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:26,250
-[Britney] Good.
-I'm Amber.

189
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:28,169
-Hey.
-I chair the dance committee.

190
00:10:28,252 --> 00:10:30,630
It's a big deal. Welcome.

191
00:10:30,713 --> 00:10:31,964
[laughs politely]

192
00:10:32,048 --> 00:10:34,842
Look, I know the school's a whole vibe,

193
00:10:34,925 --> 00:10:37,553
but you'll get used to it.
Everyone's pretty chill.

194
00:10:38,137 --> 00:10:42,850
Ah. Nice to know it's not just yacht bros
and pretentious horse girls, you know.

195
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:44,018
[laughs]

196
00:10:44,101 --> 00:10:45,102
[Teagan] No?

197
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:48,731
I'm the captain of the equestrian team.

198
00:10:50,775 --> 00:10:56,322
-Which is great. And really impressive.
-Teagan! There you are! Yeah.

199
00:10:56,405 --> 00:10:59,533
Come with me if you wanna live.
Britney. Amber.

200
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:01,118
Wow, that is the fastest

201
00:11:01,202 --> 00:11:03,537
I've ever seen anyone
unalive their social standing.

202
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:06,082
How am I supposed to know
there would be horses?

203
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:09,835
What school doesn't have horses?

204
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:12,880
I'm your first-aid buddy, Juliet Morny.

205
00:11:12,963 --> 00:11:17,510
-Hey. So is Britney, like…
-The most popular girl at school? Yeah.

206
00:11:17,593 --> 00:11:19,303
She's smart, beautiful,

207
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:22,139
voted most likely to win
in a land war in Asia.

208
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:25,393
-That's terrifying.
-Ah, it's Easton Prep.

209
00:11:25,476 --> 00:11:28,104
We're too well-heeled to be well-adjusted.

210
00:11:28,604 --> 00:11:31,440
The prestigious school's
been around since 1798.

211
00:11:31,524 --> 00:11:33,693
It's known as the Harvard of high schools.

212
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:36,529
Looks like the place where Swedish royalty
send their kids to lay low.

213
00:11:36,612 --> 00:11:38,239
We don't have Swedish.

214
00:11:38,322 --> 00:11:40,991
Prince of Spain goes here, though.
You wanna meet Federico?

215
00:11:41,075 --> 00:11:42,284
No, that's fine.

216
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:45,871
That's the Sutton House dormitory, where
you'll find me and the other boarders.

217
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:49,792
You are a day student, right? A townie?

218
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:54,255
Parking lot's over there for commuters.
Unless you're coming in by helicopter.

219
00:11:58,884 --> 00:12:03,764
It looks like a Skarsgård convention.
Who's the guy in the blazer?

220
00:12:04,348 --> 00:12:08,144
That is Josh Regis.
Sixth-generation Easton Prep kid.

221
00:12:08,227 --> 00:12:10,396
He was prom king when he was a freshman.

222
00:12:10,479 --> 00:12:14,275
That's his cousin and sidekick Ryder.
He's made out with half the girls,

223
00:12:14,358 --> 00:12:16,235
which isn't as many as it sounds.

224
00:12:16,736 --> 00:12:18,362
This used to be an all-boys, right?

225
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:20,906
They only started admitting girls
two years ago.

226
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:23,659
Great if you're straight.
Less cheer for the queer.

227
00:12:23,743 --> 00:12:27,329
-Yo, J, hook me up with that fresh meat.
-You are gross.

228
00:12:27,413 --> 00:12:29,123
-Yo!
-That is Liam.

229
00:12:29,206 --> 00:12:31,417
He made a fortune in crypto last year.

230
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:34,128
Looks like the summer break
did not crack the ego.

231
00:12:34,754 --> 00:12:36,839
Avoid him. At all cost.

232
00:12:36,922 --> 00:12:38,215
[school bell ringing]

233
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:40,301
We better get to class.

234
00:12:47,141 --> 00:12:50,853
[Ella, softly] I was a client manager
for my husband's hotels,

235
00:12:50,936 --> 00:12:54,148
and I think I can be an asset.

236
00:12:54,231 --> 00:12:55,316
-Hi!
-Hi!

237
00:12:56,066 --> 00:12:56,901
Ella?

238
00:12:57,985 --> 00:13:00,029
Ella… Emerson?

239
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:02,740
I haven't been Emerson in a…

240
00:13:02,823 --> 00:13:04,366
Wait a minute!

241
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:07,661
-Heather Wilson?
-Oh, my God!

242
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:10,206
I read all about you in <i>New York Magazine</i>.

243
00:13:10,289 --> 00:13:12,708
Oh, my God, that article
was, like, ten years ago.

244
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:15,002
That photo of you lying by the pool.

245
00:13:15,085 --> 00:13:18,464
Of course you'd be the one
to make it out of Eagle's Cove.

246
00:13:19,006 --> 00:13:21,258
What are you doing back?

247
00:13:22,843 --> 00:13:24,178
I'm shopping.

248
00:13:28,098 --> 00:13:29,642
I need this.

249
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:32,478
[teacher] Hello, young poets.

250
00:13:32,561 --> 00:13:36,148
We're going to be talking
about Byron's poem "She Walks in Beauty."

251
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:38,275
{\an8}Byron was a snacc.

252
00:13:38,359 --> 00:13:40,528
We'll read aloud
to get a feel for the language.

253
00:13:40,611 --> 00:13:42,196
-Any takers?
-[Ryder laughing]

254
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:46,200
Mr. Regis, in case you didn't realize,
class starts at the bell.

255
00:13:46,283 --> 00:13:48,118
I'm really sorry, Mr. Wu.

256
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:50,621
I would have been on time, except…

257
00:13:50,704 --> 00:13:52,581
-I didn't want to be.
-[students laughing]

258
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:55,501
Do all the hot ones
turn out to be entitled assholes?

259
00:13:55,584 --> 00:13:57,253
It's a flaw of evolution.

260
00:13:57,336 --> 00:14:00,005
It's my bad. I didn't bring the book.

261
00:14:00,506 --> 00:14:02,258
Will someone share with Josh?

262
00:14:09,014 --> 00:14:10,808
Ah. Sweet! [clears throat]

263
00:14:11,433 --> 00:14:12,434
Thanks.

264
00:14:15,437 --> 00:14:16,480
[Josh clears throat]

265
00:14:18,274 --> 00:14:20,776
<i>She walks in beauty, like the night</i>

266
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:23,571
-[soft music playing]
<i>-Of cloudless climes and starry skies</i>

267
00:14:24,071 --> 00:14:26,448
<i>And all that's best of dark and bright</i>

268
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:30,119
<i>Meet in her aspect and her eyes</i>

269
00:14:30,202 --> 00:14:32,705
[Wu] What do you think it means?

270
00:14:33,289 --> 00:14:35,165
Miss Tao? Mr. Regis?

271
00:14:36,083 --> 00:14:37,626
I think Byron was trying to smash.

272
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:44,258
Mr. Regis, if only you'd put in
as much effort into your English class

273
00:14:44,341 --> 00:14:46,552
as your rowing,
you'd actually get somewhere.

274
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:48,137
Rowing?

275
00:14:49,013 --> 00:14:50,598
Do you know where the boathouse is?

276
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:52,516
-[knocking]
-[man] Wanted to see me?

277
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:56,312
Coach Hayden. The Haverford Cup
is not far away. Are we ready?

278
00:14:56,395 --> 00:15:00,232
It's too early to say.
There's a new crop from the junior boat.

279
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:01,609
Takes time to gel.

280
00:15:01,692 --> 00:15:03,569
There's a legacy here, Coach Hayden,

281
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:05,905
which you upheld when you went here.

282
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:12,828
When I hired you, you promised
that you would get us back to the top.

283
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:15,205
-When's that gonna happen?
-It takes time to build.

284
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:16,957
We have very invested parents

285
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:19,418
who are contributing a lot
to the rowing program.

286
00:15:19,501 --> 00:15:21,795
Mm-hmm. Contributing or interfering?

287
00:15:21,879 --> 00:15:25,007
Yes, I'm very aware
of their generous donations.

288
00:15:25,090 --> 00:15:30,054
But if the parents want success,
they're gonna need to back off.

289
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:33,891
Now I know what you're asking,
and it's non-negotiable.

290
00:15:33,974 --> 00:15:38,103
He stays where he is.
But the same can't be guaranteed for you.

291
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:40,022
It's the last year of your contract.

292
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:41,732
I noticed.

293
00:15:42,566 --> 00:15:43,776
I need results, Coach.

294
00:15:43,859 --> 00:15:45,778
Yeah, good talk.

295
00:16:10,427 --> 00:16:17,267
[quiet, intriguing music playing]

296
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:40,082
[door opens]

297
00:16:40,165 --> 00:16:42,001
[indistinct chatter]

298
00:16:42,084 --> 00:16:43,919
[Ryder] Is that pre-workout
still in the fridge?

299
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:45,671
-[boy] See what I'm saying?
-[Josh] All yours.

300
00:16:45,754 --> 00:16:48,257
[woman] All right, boys,
drop your stuff quickly, please.

301
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,092
-It's erg time.
-Yes, ma'am.

302
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:51,385
[woman] Thank you.

303
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:55,472
-Hi, can I help you?
-Oh!

304
00:16:55,556 --> 00:16:57,474
Sorry. [laughs] Uh, Um…

305
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:01,311
I was looking
for the schedule for the girls' team.

306
00:17:01,395 --> 00:17:03,272
Are you Coach Hayden?

307
00:17:03,355 --> 00:17:05,107
I'm Lana, the assistant coach.

308
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:07,818
Hayden's in a meeting.
We don't have a girls' team.

309
00:17:07,901 --> 00:17:08,902
[exhales]

310
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:12,072
-Seriously? Are…
-Well, we wanted to.

311
00:17:12,156 --> 00:17:15,284
But there weren't enough girls interested.
Or any.

312
00:17:15,367 --> 00:17:17,161
We've only been coed for two years.

313
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:20,497
Well, there's interest now.
I am a lightweight sculler.

314
00:17:20,581 --> 00:17:22,291
I'm really sorry, but one is not enough.

315
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:25,544
Can I at least train here?

316
00:17:25,627 --> 00:17:28,714
Listen, you can't use the facilities
if you're not on the rowing team.

317
00:17:28,797 --> 00:17:32,051
But there is a rowing club
a few towns over.

318
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:33,552
Membership's only 5,000 a year.

319
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:35,179
Good luck.

320
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:43,812
-Hi. How'd it go?
-Hi!

321
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:45,230
[Teagan groans]

322
00:17:45,314 --> 00:17:47,566
[Ella] Oh, come on.
Don't do the teen thing.

323
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:49,860
Just actually tell me how it went.

324
00:17:49,943 --> 00:17:54,156
Okay. Uh… Classes are fine,
and people are weird.

325
00:17:55,824 --> 00:17:57,242
And there's no girls' crew.

326
00:17:57,326 --> 00:17:59,161
That's disappointing.

327
00:17:59,912 --> 00:18:02,456
Maybe you can find another sport?

328
00:18:02,539 --> 00:18:03,540
[scoffs]

329
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:06,960
You really don't get it, do you?

330
00:18:07,544 --> 00:18:08,921
What is this?

331
00:18:11,006 --> 00:18:13,175
Mom? Are you hiding this?

332
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:15,135
-No!
-Mom!

333
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:17,888
-I was--
-$250?

334
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:20,474
-But I was gonna tell you. I--
-Take it back!

335
00:18:20,557 --> 00:18:22,309
You can't put it on the credit card!

336
00:18:22,392 --> 00:18:24,228
Hey, it's my credit card!

337
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:26,063
Argh!

338
00:18:26,146 --> 00:18:30,234
["Keep Moving" by MØ playing]

339
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:33,737
<i>♪ Uh, uh, uh ♪</i>

340
00:18:33,821 --> 00:18:36,198
<i>♪ Gotta go far</i>
<i>Gotta be rich and be a rock star ♪</i>

341
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:38,325
<i>♪ Gotta have kids, get a big car ♪</i>

342
00:18:38,408 --> 00:18:40,702
<i>♪ Follow your heart into the darkness ♪</i>

343
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:44,039
<i>♪ Go, you don't wanna blow</i>
<i>And this circus waits for no one ♪</i>

344
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:45,874
<i>♪ Don't ask, don't relax ♪</i>

345
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:48,127
<i>♪ "Am I gonna crash?"</i>
<i>No, you won't, just ♪</i>

346
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:49,503
<i>♪ Ahh! ♪</i>

347
00:18:55,342 --> 00:18:56,635
[song fades]

348
00:18:57,219 --> 00:18:58,137
[exclaims]

349
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:07,062
["Circling" by Tiny Habits playing]

350
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:23,078
<i>♪ Everything's circling around us ♪</i>

351
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:28,500
<i>♪ And promising a lifetime of love ♪</i>

352
00:19:29,126 --> 00:19:34,756
<i>♪ However many times, it isn't enough ♪</i>

353
00:19:35,507 --> 00:19:41,930
<i>♪ I love you, I love you, I love you ♪</i>

354
00:19:42,014 --> 00:19:44,016
[song ends]

355
00:19:45,517 --> 00:19:48,645
Mm. Teagan, can I drive you in?
I thought we could talk.

356
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:51,023
Uh, I don't need a ride, thanks.

357
00:19:54,568 --> 00:19:56,153
[school bell ringing]

358
00:19:56,236 --> 00:19:59,239
Rowing's a bust.
What other sports do you have here?

359
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:01,116
Tennis.

360
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:03,452
Polo. Water polo.

361
00:20:04,328 --> 00:20:06,455
[Teagan] I see.
Don't you have any real sports?

362
00:20:06,538 --> 00:20:08,290
-Yeah. We have…
-[Teagan] Horses.

363
00:20:08,373 --> 00:20:09,416
-Hey, new girl.
-Yes.

364
00:20:09,499 --> 00:20:11,376
-Sounds fun.
-Did you get one of these?

365
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:13,795
No. What is that?

366
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:16,882
It's, uh, for girls
who are up for a little fun.

367
00:20:17,382 --> 00:20:18,425
Are you fun?

368
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:19,927
New girl.

369
00:20:21,678 --> 00:20:22,679
Me?

370
00:20:23,764 --> 00:20:25,849
No, and never with you.

371
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:30,229
Hi! Hi, babe.

372
00:20:30,729 --> 00:20:31,730
Hey.

373
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:39,321
Excuse me.

374
00:20:42,157 --> 00:20:43,242
He's dating Britney.

375
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:45,327
Since freshman year,
Easton's power couple.

376
00:20:45,410 --> 00:20:48,497
I can't tell if I'd do both or neither.

377
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:51,667
How can someone be so compelling
and repulsive at the same time?

378
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:53,710
[Juliet] It's a betrayal of the loins.

379
00:20:53,794 --> 00:20:55,671
Do not make an enemy of those two.

380
00:20:55,754 --> 00:20:58,507
Making enemies with beautiful people,
such a waste.

381
00:21:01,009 --> 00:21:02,636
Ah! The Town.

382
00:21:02,719 --> 00:21:05,681
They throw a big party
down at the waterfront every year.

383
00:21:05,764 --> 00:21:06,807
Are you going?

384
00:21:06,890 --> 00:21:12,646
I prefer my nights without keg stands,
but hey, I'd consider. You?

385
00:21:12,729 --> 00:21:16,441
[woman on PA] <i>Teagan Tao. Report to</i>
<i>the Head of School's Office immediately.</i>

386
00:21:16,525 --> 00:21:19,486
-Ooh, someone's in trouble.
-[tense music playing]

387
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:28,829
[Cabrera] Breaking and entering are not
becoming of an Easton Prep student.

388
00:21:28,912 --> 00:21:32,833
To be fair, it was mostly just entering
and very minimal breaking.

389
00:21:32,916 --> 00:21:33,792
Hardly the point.

390
00:21:33,875 --> 00:21:37,004
You know how dangerous it is
to go out on the water by yourself.

391
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:39,214
-I'll be calling your mother.
-[exhales]

392
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:41,675
-Am I getting expelled?
-No. No.

393
00:21:42,384 --> 00:21:43,802
But you're gonna wish you were.

394
00:21:49,725 --> 00:21:52,728
Hey, dock wench. You missed a spot.

395
00:21:53,729 --> 00:21:54,980
I heard you were into crew.

396
00:21:55,063 --> 00:21:57,441
Why don't I take you out tonight?
You can show me your stroke.

397
00:21:57,524 --> 00:22:01,778
Mm, I can't. I have plans
to vomit profusely at that idea.

398
00:22:01,862 --> 00:22:03,947
You always had a way with ladies, Liam.

399
00:22:04,531 --> 00:22:05,949
Don't talk to me, Faid.

400
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:11,788
-Hi.
-You good?

401
00:22:11,872 --> 00:22:12,998
So you go to Easton.

402
00:22:13,081 --> 00:22:14,124
Yeah.

403
00:22:14,207 --> 00:22:15,834
-And you're a rower.
-Yeah.

404
00:22:15,917 --> 00:22:17,294
What's a faid?

405
00:22:17,794 --> 00:22:20,130
It's short for "financial aid."

406
00:22:20,630 --> 00:22:23,884
I'm a scholarship kid.
They love to remind me of it.

407
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:27,888
That's not okay.

408
00:22:28,764 --> 00:22:29,973
It is what it is.

409
00:22:36,271 --> 00:22:38,065
So this is rowing.

410
00:22:40,275 --> 00:22:41,610
I see why you come.

411
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:46,573
-[Liam] Okay. Places. Here we go.
-[Teagan] Interesting seat assignments.

412
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:48,658
Here's the deal.

413
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:50,243
Every seat in the boat has a job,

414
00:22:50,327 --> 00:22:53,288
but the seat that matters most
is the stroke seat.

415
00:22:53,372 --> 00:22:56,750
Otherwise known as "eight seat,"
where you put your best rower.

416
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:58,418
Or in this case, Josh.

417
00:22:58,919 --> 00:23:03,173
Next, in seven seat.
So close to stroke and yet so far away.

418
00:23:03,256 --> 00:23:06,927
Then comes the engine room.
The six, five, four, and three.

419
00:23:07,010 --> 00:23:09,179
-Those are the powerhouses.
-[Liam] Where's your cable?

420
00:23:09,262 --> 00:23:10,847
Then there's bow pair, and they…

421
00:23:11,807 --> 00:23:13,600
-um…
-[Liam] Is this hard?

422
00:23:13,683 --> 00:23:15,352
…have good technique.

423
00:23:16,686 --> 00:23:18,105
The weaklings.

424
00:23:18,188 --> 00:23:20,023
Why does Liam get a free ride?

425
00:23:20,107 --> 00:23:21,733
-[Teagan] He's the cox.
-Excuse me?

426
00:23:21,817 --> 00:23:26,154
[laughing] Short for coxswain.
It's the name of the position.

427
00:23:26,238 --> 00:23:27,739
[suggestively] Oh.

428
00:23:27,823 --> 00:23:29,533
We're gonna have to move past this.

429
00:23:30,117 --> 00:23:32,953
[Liam] Know how hard it is to do this job
when you guys can't get together?

430
00:23:33,036 --> 00:23:34,788
Follow the stroke's pace!

431
00:23:34,871 --> 00:23:38,667
-Yo, we're on Josh!
-[energetic music playing]

432
00:23:38,750 --> 00:23:40,252
You're already tired!

433
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:44,923
Drive! Drive!

434
00:23:45,006 --> 00:23:48,427
Legs! Legs! Legs! Legs! Josh!

435
00:23:49,052 --> 00:23:50,053
[Lana] Time.

436
00:23:51,179 --> 00:23:53,056
I swear… Again!

437
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:55,642
[Lian] Josh! Your puddles are shit.

438
00:23:55,725 --> 00:23:58,478
-Yeah, yeah, man. I got it.
-[Liam] Do something! Do you?

439
00:23:58,562 --> 00:24:00,856
This is basic stuff.

440
00:24:00,939 --> 00:24:03,150
-Did they get worse?
-I'm telling you.

441
00:24:04,901 --> 00:24:06,820
I can't believe this. Again!

442
00:24:06,903 --> 00:24:10,198
-You're literally jelly legs, bro.
-Just piss off.

443
00:24:12,576 --> 00:24:13,618
[oarlock rattling]

444
00:24:13,702 --> 00:24:15,829
-[rower] Whoa!
-[Liam] Oh, my God!

445
00:24:15,912 --> 00:24:16,872
[rower 2] What the fuck?

446
00:24:16,955 --> 00:24:19,040
I'm good. Sorry. My bad.

447
00:24:19,124 --> 00:24:20,792
-Ugh.
-Ouch.

448
00:24:20,876 --> 00:24:24,713
That's what you call catching a crab.
And that will kill your run.

449
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:29,843
And now the debrief.

450
00:24:29,926 --> 00:24:32,345
-Less sweating, more strategy.
-[Liam] And up.

451
00:24:32,929 --> 00:24:34,514
[Juliet] Is there going to be crying?

452
00:24:34,598 --> 00:24:35,974
-[Liam] Down.
-[Teagan] Probably not.

453
00:24:36,057 --> 00:24:37,184
[Juliet] Boring.

454
00:24:37,267 --> 00:24:38,351
[Liam] Walk it out.

455
00:24:38,852 --> 00:24:40,145
I'm out.

456
00:24:41,146 --> 00:24:42,314
-Bye.
-Mm.

457
00:24:49,738 --> 00:24:53,200
-[Liam] Yo, Crabcatcher! What was that?
-[Josh] Your calls are no good either.

458
00:24:53,283 --> 00:24:55,744
[Liam] Yeah, says the guy
who can't get the stroke rate up.

459
00:24:57,245 --> 00:24:59,247
[Lana] Well, that could have gone better.

460
00:24:59,748 --> 00:25:02,167
[Hayden] I'm thinking we drop Ryder,
pull up Cam.

461
00:25:03,001 --> 00:25:05,086
Ryder's not the problem, though.

462
00:25:06,421 --> 00:25:07,422
Excuse me?

463
00:25:08,924 --> 00:25:10,592
Don't drop Ryder down. It's unfair.

464
00:25:10,675 --> 00:25:13,762
He's not rowing well
because he's trying to match Josh.

465
00:25:13,845 --> 00:25:16,890
Josh wasn't pulling enough.
Look at his puddles, you should…

466
00:25:18,975 --> 00:25:20,185
swap him.

467
00:25:20,268 --> 00:25:22,020
All right.
Who would you put on the throne?

468
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:25,482
Cam has the best technique
and he's working the hardest,

469
00:25:25,565 --> 00:25:31,071
but, uh, the team's not a fan of his.
So, it's the big guy in six.

470
00:25:31,154 --> 00:25:32,239
-Bronson.
-Baloo.

471
00:25:32,322 --> 00:25:34,616
Yeah. Dunno if he has the brains,
but he's got the brawn,

472
00:25:34,699 --> 00:25:37,327
and he's got the team's love,
which you need

473
00:25:37,410 --> 00:25:40,539
because your coxie's lost the team.

474
00:25:40,622 --> 00:25:41,915
Astute.

475
00:25:43,708 --> 00:25:46,044
-What do you think? You wanna switch Josh?
-Who, me?

476
00:25:46,127 --> 00:25:48,672
-Yeah.
-I would like to keep my job. Thank you.

477
00:25:49,172 --> 00:25:52,008
I won't have one to worry about soon
if we don't start winning, no?

478
00:25:55,971 --> 00:25:57,305
Boys. Back in the water.

479
00:25:57,389 --> 00:26:00,058
Last setup of the day,
but we're gonna change it up.

480
00:26:00,141 --> 00:26:04,813
Baloo, you're in eight. Ryder, seven.
Cam, six. Josh, bow.

481
00:26:04,896 --> 00:26:06,856
[tense music playing]

482
00:26:06,940 --> 00:26:08,316
Holy shit!

483
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:10,694
-What the hell?
-We're trying something out.

484
00:26:10,777 --> 00:26:12,862
-Coach, you can't do this.
-[Hayden] Get in the boat.

485
00:26:14,322 --> 00:26:15,657
You can't do this.

486
00:26:16,157 --> 00:26:17,909
Get in the boat.

487
00:26:17,993 --> 00:26:20,745
[tense music continues]

488
00:26:25,041 --> 00:26:26,501
All right, let's go, ladies.

489
00:26:28,670 --> 00:26:30,589
[Liam] All right, everybody ready?

490
00:26:30,672 --> 00:26:33,883
-[rower] Yes, sir.
-[Liam] All right, listen up. And row.

491
00:26:40,557 --> 00:26:43,893
Come on, boys. Let's go, let's go!

492
00:26:45,645 --> 00:26:48,565
Come on. Let's go. Whoo!

493
00:26:49,190 --> 00:26:51,401
[Liam] You want it? You got your shot.

494
00:26:53,737 --> 00:26:54,821
[stopwatch beeping]

495
00:26:56,197 --> 00:26:57,324
Shaved eight seconds.

496
00:26:57,407 --> 00:27:01,578
Give me some. Give me some.
Give me some. Let's go, bro!

497
00:27:01,661 --> 00:27:03,496
-See that shit? Whoo!
-[Cam] Come on, Baloo.

498
00:27:10,128 --> 00:27:11,838
Hey! You.

499
00:27:12,339 --> 00:27:13,632
What is your problem?

500
00:27:13,715 --> 00:27:15,425
-Me?
-Yeah.

501
00:27:15,508 --> 00:27:18,053
Yeah, I saw you talking to the coach.

502
00:27:18,136 --> 00:27:21,473
I've been in stroke seat since I've been
at this school. Suddenly I'm down to bow?

503
00:27:21,556 --> 00:27:23,308
Maybe you're not the best rower.

504
00:27:23,391 --> 00:27:26,186
Maybe you're not pulling your weight.

505
00:27:26,269 --> 00:27:29,814
Maybe you should keep your head
in the boat instead of up your ass.

506
00:27:29,898 --> 00:27:30,857
[laughs]

507
00:27:30,940 --> 00:27:33,151
-Who do you think you are?
-Who the hell are you?

508
00:27:33,234 --> 00:27:34,319
Oh.

509
00:27:35,236 --> 00:27:36,488
Oh, I'm Josh Regis.

510
00:27:37,822 --> 00:27:38,823
Watch yourself.

511
00:27:39,532 --> 00:27:40,450
[Teagan laughs]

512
00:27:41,242 --> 00:27:42,160
[snaps]

513
00:27:43,953 --> 00:27:45,955
["300 Dreams" by After playing]

514
00:27:51,586 --> 00:27:53,963
<i>♪ Oh, look at the state of me ♪</i>

515
00:27:54,047 --> 00:27:55,006
[object snaps]

516
00:27:55,090 --> 00:27:57,258
[Teagan sighs] No…

517
00:27:58,051 --> 00:28:01,262
<i>♪ …falling down ♪</i>

518
00:28:01,346 --> 00:28:04,599
<i>♪ Oh, look at the state of me ♪</i>

519
00:28:04,683 --> 00:28:11,064
<i>♪ I'm always falling down ♪</i>

520
00:28:16,152 --> 00:28:18,988
-Hey.
-[Cam] Ever think biking's not your thing?

521
00:28:20,782 --> 00:28:21,950
Tire's toast.

522
00:28:26,663 --> 00:28:28,998
-I heard Josh ream you out.
-Mm.

523
00:28:29,874 --> 00:28:31,334
Or you reamed him out.

524
00:28:32,585 --> 00:28:34,587
Not my smartest move.

525
00:28:35,964 --> 00:28:37,924
Easton Prep is a hard crowd.

526
00:28:38,425 --> 00:28:41,261
They'll do everything they can
to make you feel like you're less.

527
00:28:41,344 --> 00:28:42,345
You're not.

528
00:28:43,179 --> 00:28:44,305
Don't back down.

529
00:28:58,653 --> 00:29:00,864
Everyone's going
to the dock party tonight.

530
00:29:01,906 --> 00:29:04,200
-I heard.
-But you should go.

531
00:29:04,284 --> 00:29:06,536
There's more to the Cove
than the Easton snobs.

532
00:29:06,619 --> 00:29:08,663
I'll, uh, think about it.

533
00:29:09,748 --> 00:29:11,833
I'm… I have an extra wristband.

534
00:29:12,500 --> 00:29:14,252
Text me if you want it.

535
00:29:18,465 --> 00:29:19,466
Maybe I'll see you later.

536
00:29:20,300 --> 00:29:21,217
Let's get your bike.

537
00:29:21,301 --> 00:29:24,387
[soft music playing]

538
00:29:41,988 --> 00:29:45,450
Oh… This is a knockoff.

539
00:29:45,533 --> 00:29:47,786
Ah! For drag.

540
00:29:47,869 --> 00:29:50,413
Or for burning. Nothing in between.

541
00:29:50,497 --> 00:29:53,875
-Juliet, I don't need a donate pile.
-[laughs] It's adorable you think so.

542
00:29:53,958 --> 00:29:57,253
You're not working a club girl working
bottle service on the Sunset Strip.

543
00:29:57,337 --> 00:30:01,216
-Hey, that's cute.
-It reeks of effort.

544
00:30:01,299 --> 00:30:03,635
And the one unwritten rule of Easton Prep

545
00:30:03,718 --> 00:30:05,386
is never look like you're trying.

546
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:06,471
[Teagan] Can't I a little?

547
00:30:06,554 --> 00:30:08,181
[Siri] <i>You have one notification.</i>

548
00:30:08,681 --> 00:30:09,849
<i>Message from Kesha.</i>

549
00:30:09,933 --> 00:30:12,143
<i>-Would you like to open it?</i>
-Ignore.

550
00:30:12,227 --> 00:30:14,854
-Sorry… what?
-[Juliet] It's not what you think.

551
00:30:14,938 --> 00:30:17,941
When my parents have bad news,
they share it by celebrity messenger.

552
00:30:18,024 --> 00:30:19,526
They think it'll soften the blow.

553
00:30:19,609 --> 00:30:21,277
Juliet, that's amazing.

554
00:30:21,361 --> 00:30:23,822
Until Zendaya tells you
your grandmother's passed away.

555
00:30:23,905 --> 00:30:25,114
Please open it.

556
00:30:25,198 --> 00:30:26,741
Only if you try this on.

557
00:30:30,036 --> 00:30:30,912
[Juliet] Mm-hmm.

558
00:30:30,995 --> 00:30:32,664
-I don't know.
-You can trust me.

559
00:30:32,747 --> 00:30:35,333
I don't know. Isn't it a little short?

560
00:30:35,834 --> 00:30:38,336
[over recording] <i>Hey, Juliet,</i>
<i>it's your girl Kesha.</i>

561
00:30:38,419 --> 00:30:41,047
<i>I heard from your mom</i>
<i>that it is your birthday.</i>

562
00:30:41,130 --> 00:30:44,008
<i>So happy birthday, bitch.</i>

563
00:30:44,092 --> 00:30:47,428
<i>We all know</i>
<i>it's not a party until I walk in.</i>

564
00:30:48,137 --> 00:30:50,974
<i>And your parents wanted me to let you know</i>

565
00:30:51,057 --> 00:30:54,853
<i>that I'm not going to be walking in,</i>
<i>and neither are they.</i>

566
00:30:55,436 --> 00:30:56,771
<i>Bummer. I kno--</i>

567
00:30:57,689 --> 00:31:00,066
-Harsh.
-Happy birthday?

568
00:31:00,149 --> 00:31:04,195
They love that I'm 3,500 miles away.
I'm easier to forget.

569
00:31:04,988 --> 00:31:08,533
But enough melodrama.
We need a hair curler.

570
00:31:08,616 --> 00:31:11,911
I think it's in one of the boxes.
Maybe it's in my mom's room.

571
00:31:11,995 --> 00:31:13,162
One sec.

572
00:31:19,794 --> 00:31:21,254
[intriguing music playing]

573
00:31:21,337 --> 00:31:22,505
What the hell?

574
00:31:24,966 --> 00:31:28,261
It's my dad's stuff.
She was hiding it in her hamper.

575
00:31:28,803 --> 00:31:32,724
-Dad's not in the picture?
-No, I… I don't know why she has it.

576
00:31:32,807 --> 00:31:36,394
Uh… Hey, do you think
we can finish changing in your dorm?

577
00:31:36,477 --> 00:31:37,687
Of course.

578
00:31:37,770 --> 00:31:38,897
Okay.

579
00:31:40,607 --> 00:31:42,108
All families are weird.

580
00:31:46,613 --> 00:31:48,656
-[sighs]
-[footsteps approaching]

581
00:31:48,740 --> 00:31:50,742
[Ella] Hey. Where are you going?

582
00:31:51,826 --> 00:31:53,202
Out.

583
00:31:53,286 --> 00:31:55,121
[Ella] I-is everything okay?

584
00:31:56,164 --> 00:31:57,874
[exhales] No.

585
00:32:03,963 --> 00:32:06,633
[melancholy music playing]

586
00:32:07,467 --> 00:32:10,470
-[seagull calling]
-[distant ship horn blaring]

587
00:32:15,683 --> 00:32:18,394
[man] Yeah, so I told them,
"You're being shellfish!"

588
00:32:18,478 --> 00:32:20,563
-[man 2] Yeah, that's really good.
-[woman] Amazing.

589
00:32:20,647 --> 00:32:23,107
[woman 2] All right,
they better have a good crab salad.

590
00:32:23,191 --> 00:32:24,025
Jim.

591
00:32:25,109 --> 00:32:26,319
-[laughs]
-Ella!

592
00:32:27,445 --> 00:32:28,821
[Jim] Hang on. [laughs]

593
00:32:28,905 --> 00:32:29,781
Uh, table nine.

594
00:32:32,241 --> 00:32:34,243
[both laughing]

595
00:32:34,953 --> 00:32:39,874
Well, if it isn't Miss Eagle's Cove 2003.
Ella Emerson, how the heck are you?

596
00:32:39,958 --> 00:32:40,833
I'm broke.

597
00:32:42,335 --> 00:32:44,170
I have no idea where my husband is.

598
00:32:44,253 --> 00:32:47,840
I sold everything I had
to buy a car to get out of town.

599
00:32:47,924 --> 00:32:50,343
And my daughter hates me.

600
00:32:51,719 --> 00:32:52,553
I messed up.

601
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:55,223
Come on. You gotta buck up. Life goes on.

602
00:32:55,306 --> 00:32:57,266
You always hated David.

603
00:32:57,350 --> 00:32:59,394
-And you were right.
-I liked the other guy better.

604
00:33:00,144 --> 00:33:01,688
Eh… I'll pour another.

605
00:33:02,605 --> 00:33:04,857
Oh, sorry, get back to work.
You're in the weeds.

606
00:33:05,483 --> 00:33:07,360
We've been short ever since Jane retired.

607
00:33:07,443 --> 00:33:10,071
I don't know how many more
of these shifts I can take.

608
00:33:10,154 --> 00:33:11,406
You want me to go back there?

609
00:33:11,990 --> 00:33:16,160
-Don't play me.
-No, Jim. I-I… I need a job.

610
00:33:16,744 --> 00:33:18,121
Can I come back?

611
00:33:20,289 --> 00:33:21,624
You close tonight.

612
00:33:21,708 --> 00:33:23,626
["Truth of Pursuit"
by Sarah Kinsley playing]

613
00:33:30,341 --> 00:33:31,592
-[tires screech]
-[engine roars]

614
00:33:31,676 --> 00:33:34,846
<i>♪ …baby, you were mine ♪</i>

615
00:33:35,430 --> 00:33:39,934
<i>♪ I think about it</i>
<i>Almost every night on the line ♪</i>

616
00:33:40,435 --> 00:33:44,480
<i>♪ Do you ever wonder</i>
<i>How our stars will align? ♪</i>

617
00:33:44,981 --> 00:33:45,815
[Juliet laughs]

618
00:33:46,607 --> 00:33:48,818
[Teagan squeals, laughs excitedly]

619
00:33:51,404 --> 00:33:52,405
Wow.

620
00:33:56,242 --> 00:34:00,496
Well, if my mom grounds me,
I hope the party's worth it.

621
00:34:00,580 --> 00:34:03,750
[Juliet] She cares enough to ground you.
More than some of us get.

622
00:34:03,833 --> 00:34:06,961
[Teagan] You don't get grounded?
You're not trying hard enough.

623
00:34:07,045 --> 00:34:10,548
[Juliet] That would mean they'd have to
take a minute away from their own lives.

624
00:34:11,049 --> 00:34:12,717
Count your blessings.

625
00:34:14,302 --> 00:34:18,556
<i>♪ Oh, I wanna feel alive ♪</i>

626
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:23,227
<i>♪ Like I did, like I used to ♪</i>

627
00:34:23,311 --> 00:34:26,064
<i>♪ And oh… ♪</i>

628
00:34:26,147 --> 00:34:27,774
Well, look who showed up.

629
00:34:28,566 --> 00:34:29,984
Here's your wristband.

630
00:34:34,614 --> 00:34:36,115
Well, have a good time.

631
00:34:37,867 --> 00:34:40,036
Oh, you… Uh, you weren't…

632
00:34:40,119 --> 00:34:44,624
Actually, I have to…
go take care of a few things.

633
00:34:44,707 --> 00:34:46,459
-[laughs]
-[Juliet] You two go ahead.

634
00:34:49,003 --> 00:34:50,797
[Teagan] Okay. Huh.

635
00:34:51,756 --> 00:34:54,050
Okay, come on. Let's get a drink.

636
00:34:54,592 --> 00:34:58,012
["No Broke Boys"
by Disco Lines and Tinashe playing]

637
00:34:58,096 --> 00:35:01,766
<i>♪ Ain't no lie, ain't no shade</i>
<i>Shame on me, then you know he paid ♪</i>

638
00:35:01,849 --> 00:35:05,436
<i>♪ Look so good, makes no sense</i>
<i>Badass bitch with my badass friends ♪</i>

639
00:35:05,520 --> 00:35:09,232
<i>♪ No broke boys, ain't no shade</i>
<i>…on me, then you know he paid ♪</i>

640
00:35:09,315 --> 00:35:11,442
<i>♪ No broke boys, no new friends… ♪</i>

641
00:35:11,526 --> 00:35:14,153
-[Josh] Oh, really now?
-[Britney laughs]

642
00:35:14,237 --> 00:35:15,613
You look so cute.

643
00:35:15,696 --> 00:35:17,281
You didn't bring your boat?

644
00:35:17,824 --> 00:35:19,700
It's out for maintenance
with my other boat.

645
00:35:19,784 --> 00:35:20,743
Mm.

646
00:35:20,827 --> 00:35:23,454
[boys laughing and clamoring]

647
00:35:26,374 --> 00:35:28,000
[Teagan] This is so shady.

648
00:35:28,543 --> 00:35:30,711
Welcome to Eagle's Cove.

649
00:35:31,420 --> 00:35:33,965
Can't really use a fake ID
when everyone knows your name.

650
00:35:34,048 --> 00:35:36,008
Isn't there practice tomorrow morning?

651
00:35:36,592 --> 00:35:37,844
It's a dock party.

652
00:35:39,137 --> 00:35:42,849
Cam, my main bear! Bro, how you doing?

653
00:35:43,349 --> 00:35:47,145
And the boat rocker.
Bro, because of you, I got upgraded.

654
00:35:47,228 --> 00:35:48,938
Uh, I didn't switch the seats.

655
00:35:49,021 --> 00:35:54,068
-No, no. But you spoke truth to power.
-Don't think that's what that means.

656
00:35:54,152 --> 00:35:56,028
Hey, hey, tequila.

657
00:35:56,529 --> 00:35:59,866
You, me, Chamomile, make three.

658
00:36:00,408 --> 00:36:01,534
Cheers, ladies.

659
00:36:02,034 --> 00:36:04,829
-Cheers.
-Cheers. Ladies.

660
00:36:07,874 --> 00:36:08,875
[giggling] Okay.

661
00:36:10,084 --> 00:36:12,086
[Teagan] Ooh. [laughing]

662
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:14,672
Well, I guess the gloves are off.

663
00:36:14,755 --> 00:36:16,799
Here I am being a gentleman,
trying not to get you drunk.

664
00:36:16,883 --> 00:36:19,594
Wow, okay, let's make it interesting.

665
00:36:20,219 --> 00:36:23,806
Get one in,
and you can drink or answer a question.

666
00:36:23,890 --> 00:36:24,891
Okay.

667
00:36:26,809 --> 00:36:28,895
-Turns out I'm a beer pong shark.
-[Teagan laughs]

668
00:36:29,770 --> 00:36:31,564
I heard you row. Are you any good?

669
00:36:31,647 --> 00:36:34,483
I was a Southwest junior champ.
I had my eyes set on Stanford.

670
00:36:34,567 --> 00:36:35,526
Stanford?

671
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:38,946
One of their scouts gave me his card
at the regatta last year.

672
00:36:39,906 --> 00:36:41,240
I was hoping for U-Dub.

673
00:36:43,534 --> 00:36:44,660
Why Stanford?

674
00:36:44,744 --> 00:36:47,663
My dad rowed for Stanford.
I thought I'd get him a Stanford cowbell

675
00:36:47,747 --> 00:36:49,290
when I got in, but, uh…

676
00:36:50,249 --> 00:36:52,960
Maybe one day
I'll make it back to California.

677
00:36:53,044 --> 00:36:55,046
[ball clatters and bounces]

678
00:36:57,465 --> 00:36:58,716
[Cam] Why'd you move?

679
00:37:00,092 --> 00:37:03,679
My dad, he… uh…

680
00:37:05,723 --> 00:37:11,187
passed away, and we needed a change.
Uh, what about you? Why U-Dub?

681
00:37:15,691 --> 00:37:16,943
Why U-Dub?

682
00:37:17,026 --> 00:37:20,154
They're a D1 crew.
I'd be on an Olympic track.

683
00:37:20,696 --> 00:37:25,701
-And there's this engineering program.
-You wanna be an Olympian and an engineer?

684
00:37:26,994 --> 00:37:27,828
Wow.

685
00:37:27,912 --> 00:37:30,206
I'd be the first in my family
to go to college.

686
00:37:31,624 --> 00:37:32,667
Don't tell anyone.

687
00:37:36,671 --> 00:37:39,465
[dance music playing]

688
00:37:41,926 --> 00:37:43,803
Tequila.

689
00:37:44,303 --> 00:37:45,930
Crew shots, come on.

690
00:37:46,013 --> 00:37:48,975
I'm not really
into tequila right now, actually.

691
00:37:50,184 --> 00:37:51,185
Fair.

692
00:37:51,269 --> 00:37:54,480
But, like… Oh don't be sore.

693
00:37:54,981 --> 00:37:57,108
The boat was faster with me.
Fair and square.

694
00:37:57,608 --> 00:37:58,609
It's fine.

695
00:38:00,152 --> 00:38:03,030
You're mad at me.
You're seriously mad at me. Okay.

696
00:38:05,199 --> 00:38:06,701
There's only one way to end this.

697
00:38:06,784 --> 00:38:09,620
-Bear hug! Come here, man.
-Okay.

698
00:38:09,704 --> 00:38:13,249
-You love this. You love me. Baloo.
-No. Dude!

699
00:38:13,332 --> 00:38:15,668
-Baloo. Yeah.
-Okay, Bronson.

700
00:38:16,168 --> 00:38:17,837
-Bye.
-I didn't do it. Okay.

701
00:38:18,462 --> 00:38:19,463
Lighten up.

702
00:38:20,256 --> 00:38:21,257
Just a little.

703
00:38:22,591 --> 00:38:24,719
Hey. Are you okay?

704
00:38:24,802 --> 00:38:28,222
Sorry. You know my brother
likes to rile you up like that. It's…

705
00:38:29,432 --> 00:38:32,685
Okay. Okay, okay. Take it easy.

706
00:38:32,768 --> 00:38:35,730
-Leave some for the rest of us.
-Can you not? That's controlling.

707
00:38:36,397 --> 00:38:37,690
What, are you mad at me?

708
00:38:38,399 --> 00:38:40,860
No. There's a lot going on, and…

709
00:38:41,360 --> 00:38:44,238
That new girl
is making me look like an asshole.

710
00:38:44,322 --> 00:38:46,240
-And--
-You're thinking about the new girl?

711
00:38:46,324 --> 00:38:48,784
-No, I'm not.
-Why are you thinking about the--

712
00:38:48,868 --> 00:38:50,703
I just need some space.

713
00:38:50,786 --> 00:38:51,787
Okay.

714
00:38:59,962 --> 00:39:02,173
Something's up with him.

715
00:39:02,715 --> 00:39:05,468
No disrespect,
but Josh can be a moody bitch.

716
00:39:05,551 --> 00:39:08,095
Hey, he's still my guy. Love and support.

717
00:39:08,179 --> 00:39:09,472
Love and support.

718
00:39:09,555 --> 00:39:11,182
We were fine,

719
00:39:11,265 --> 00:39:13,809
but ever since he got back
from training camp in Baltimore,

720
00:39:13,893 --> 00:39:15,936
he's just been acting weird.

721
00:39:16,437 --> 00:39:18,230
[Amber] Do you think something went down?

722
00:39:18,314 --> 00:39:19,690
I don't know.

723
00:39:19,774 --> 00:39:22,902
He silenced a call from a 410 number
when he thought I wasn't looking.

724
00:39:22,985 --> 00:39:24,695
That's a Baltimore area code.

725
00:39:24,779 --> 00:39:26,405
-[Amber] Uh…
-I know.

726
00:39:28,949 --> 00:39:31,619
Oh, what is she doing here?

727
00:39:31,702 --> 00:39:33,913
Oh, my God, do you know about her?

728
00:39:33,996 --> 00:39:35,206
No.

729
00:39:35,289 --> 00:39:37,416
I did a little cyberstalking.

730
00:39:38,084 --> 00:39:41,087
I found something
you might be interested in.

731
00:39:46,217 --> 00:39:48,219
-Thanks for hanging with me.
-[mic feedback squeals]

732
00:39:48,302 --> 00:39:50,179
[Britney] Hello. Hi.

733
00:39:50,262 --> 00:39:52,390
Hi, everyone. Oh, hi!

734
00:39:52,473 --> 00:39:56,519
[sighs] I just wanted to say
that you should watch your bags, people.

735
00:39:56,602 --> 00:40:02,316
This is a public service announcement.
We have a thief in our midst.

736
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:04,652
[people murmuring]

737
00:40:06,153 --> 00:40:09,782
[reporter] <i>…when it was discovered</i>
<i>that luxury hotelier, David Tao,</i>

738
00:40:09,865 --> 00:40:14,870
<i>had allegedly defrauded investors</i>
<i>out of nearly $47 million.</i>

739
00:40:14,954 --> 00:40:19,792
<i>Tao, who built the White Aspen chain</i>
<i>of boutique hotels across California,</i>

740
00:40:19,875 --> 00:40:22,294
<i>is accused of misappropriating funds</i>

741
00:40:22,378 --> 00:40:24,922
{\an8}<i>to maintain</i>
<i>the property's lavish operations</i>

742
00:40:25,005 --> 00:40:26,424
{\an8}<i>and his family's lifestyle.</i>

743
00:40:26,507 --> 00:40:27,466
Oh!

744
00:40:27,550 --> 00:40:29,927
<i>-Authorities have seized assets…</i>
-I know.

745
00:40:30,010 --> 00:40:32,138
<i>…including their home and vehicles.</i>

746
00:40:32,221 --> 00:40:33,556
<i>Tao remains at large,</i>

747
00:40:33,639 --> 00:40:36,934
<i>with federal warrants</i>
<i>issued for their arrest.</i>

748
00:40:37,017 --> 00:40:39,937
<i>The FBI is asking</i>
<i>anyone with information about…</i>

749
00:40:40,020 --> 00:40:45,025
Where's your dad, Teagan?
Where's the money? Care to comment?

750
00:40:45,526 --> 00:40:47,069
-All right, Britney.
-Oh.

751
00:40:48,070 --> 00:40:50,156
[tense music playing]

752
00:40:50,239 --> 00:40:51,949
-Is that you?
-Uh…

753
00:40:52,032 --> 00:40:53,826
-You said your dad was dead.
-[exhales]

754
00:40:53,909 --> 00:40:55,578
Did he really steal all that money?

755
00:40:56,078 --> 00:40:57,037
I, um…

756
00:40:58,330 --> 00:40:59,415
You should go.

757
00:40:59,498 --> 00:41:00,499
Okay.

758
00:41:02,042 --> 00:41:03,544
[murmuring]

759
00:41:05,754 --> 00:41:07,089
[laughs quietly]

760
00:41:14,555 --> 00:41:15,639
[sad laugh]

761
00:41:16,891 --> 00:41:18,434
What happened to you?

762
00:41:18,934 --> 00:41:23,063
I have finally figured out
how to convince my mom to come visit.

763
00:41:23,731 --> 00:41:25,441
What happened to you?

764
00:41:26,025 --> 00:41:29,195
[laughs wryly] Just a public execution.

765
00:41:30,696 --> 00:41:32,406
I don't really wanna
talk about it right now.

766
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:34,783
Well, you can tell me
when I'm back at school.

767
00:41:36,327 --> 00:41:38,621
Wait, you're not… going tomorrow?

768
00:41:38,704 --> 00:41:40,998
No, I've got to get my car fixed.

769
00:41:41,081 --> 00:41:43,501
What? What's wrong with your car?

770
00:41:43,584 --> 00:41:44,460
[gasps]

771
00:41:46,587 --> 00:41:48,005
-Wha…
-[dramatic music playing]

772
00:41:48,088 --> 00:41:49,632
Oh, my God. What are you doing?

773
00:41:49,715 --> 00:41:51,550
-You should probably get going.
-What?

774
00:41:55,137 --> 00:41:58,140
Mom, please come and get me.

775
00:42:01,852 --> 00:42:03,437
-[Teagan] Oh!
-Oh, my God.

776
00:42:03,938 --> 00:42:04,939
[Ella clears throat]

777
00:42:05,648 --> 00:42:06,649
[Teagan groans]

778
00:42:06,732 --> 00:42:08,400
-Come on, you.
-[Teagan moans]

779
00:42:08,484 --> 00:42:11,362
Hey, it's okay. [laughs]

780
00:42:11,904 --> 00:42:12,821
[Ella groans]

781
00:42:12,905 --> 00:42:14,240
-[Teagan] Yeah. Ooh…
-Oh!

782
00:42:14,323 --> 00:42:15,616
[Teagan] Oh, my God.

783
00:42:15,699 --> 00:42:16,992
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

784
00:42:17,076 --> 00:42:18,244
Sorry.

785
00:42:18,911 --> 00:42:21,330
I'm sorry. I…

786
00:42:24,250 --> 00:42:25,292
may have messed up.

787
00:42:27,711 --> 00:42:28,712
Just a little bit.

788
00:42:28,796 --> 00:42:30,214
-You did.
-I'm sorry.

789
00:42:32,591 --> 00:42:33,676
I'm glad.

790
00:42:36,595 --> 00:42:37,846
What?

791
00:42:38,347 --> 00:42:40,140
At least you're talking to me.

792
00:42:40,224 --> 00:42:45,437
Oh, okay, like you want to talk.

793
00:42:45,521 --> 00:42:47,064
Of course I do.

794
00:42:47,731 --> 00:42:49,275
[laughs]

795
00:42:49,358 --> 00:42:54,321
You can't even admit
that Dad wrecked our lives.

796
00:42:54,405 --> 00:42:56,198
Hey, that's not true. Come on.

797
00:42:56,282 --> 00:42:59,201
See? You just…
You can't talk about anything real.

798
00:42:59,285 --> 00:43:00,536
And I found his duffel bag.

799
00:43:01,328 --> 00:43:03,289
I saw that you hid it from me.

800
00:43:03,372 --> 00:43:05,416
I just want to know,
like, what do you know?

801
00:43:05,499 --> 00:43:09,378
Stop sugarcoating everything
and just tell me the truth.

802
00:43:09,461 --> 00:43:10,462
Truth?

803
00:43:10,546 --> 00:43:12,006
[emotional music playing]

804
00:43:12,089 --> 00:43:15,009
The truth is that I hate Eagle's Cove.

805
00:43:16,927 --> 00:43:20,097
Twenty years ago, I left here,
I promised I would never be back,

806
00:43:20,180 --> 00:43:21,724
and here I am.

807
00:43:21,807 --> 00:43:25,185
Because your dad just left.

808
00:43:25,269 --> 00:43:26,687
[exhaled]

809
00:43:27,855 --> 00:43:29,273
I'm not upset.

810
00:43:30,441 --> 00:43:32,484
I'm furious.

811
00:43:39,199 --> 00:43:40,701
But you know what?

812
00:43:44,997 --> 00:43:49,293
As mad as I get,
I remember he's your father.

813
00:43:52,379 --> 00:43:54,590
I still can't believe
he would do this to us.

814
00:43:57,092 --> 00:43:58,719
But he did.

815
00:44:01,305 --> 00:44:02,640
I kept his bag.

816
00:44:03,682 --> 00:44:05,017
I don't know why.

817
00:44:05,100 --> 00:44:07,978
I think I thought
maybe there'd be some answers.

818
00:44:08,062 --> 00:44:09,438
And there weren't.

819
00:44:11,190 --> 00:44:15,694
Now I don't know
whether I should hold onto it or burn it.

820
00:44:15,778 --> 00:44:17,071
[laughs]

821
00:44:17,154 --> 00:44:18,906
No. Don't.

822
00:44:20,616 --> 00:44:22,284
Don't burn it.

823
00:44:27,331 --> 00:44:29,458
I'm so angry.

824
00:44:29,541 --> 00:44:30,459
[Ella] I know.

825
00:44:30,542 --> 00:44:33,545
At him, Mom,
but I really miss him. [crying]

826
00:44:33,629 --> 00:44:35,506
Oh, God, me too.

827
00:44:36,590 --> 00:44:37,925
[Ella sighs]

828
00:44:39,093 --> 00:44:40,469
-Asshole.
-[Teagan laughs]

829
00:44:41,053 --> 00:44:43,305
[both laughing]

830
00:44:50,354 --> 00:44:53,691
[scrubbing]

831
00:44:54,817 --> 00:44:57,027
It's 15 past, where is everyone?

832
00:44:57,528 --> 00:44:59,363
Freaking dock party.

833
00:45:00,656 --> 00:45:02,324
You sure you don't wanna
scrap the boys team

834
00:45:02,408 --> 00:45:04,034
and try and round up some girls instead?

835
00:45:04,118 --> 00:45:05,869
[laughs] That's a nice try.

836
00:45:05,953 --> 00:45:08,038
Easton's never gonna make
a big push for a girls' team

837
00:45:08,122 --> 00:45:09,331
until the boys start winning.

838
00:45:09,415 --> 00:45:12,167
-Hey, go give me a quick lap.
-Just… Yeah, one second.

839
00:45:12,251 --> 00:45:13,585
You are the coxswain of this team.

840
00:45:13,669 --> 00:45:15,963
-You're supposed to lead it.
-I said give me a minute.

841
00:45:16,046 --> 00:45:18,841
No wonder you're losing.

842
00:45:18,924 --> 00:45:20,008
Excuse me?

843
00:45:21,343 --> 00:45:23,095
You're here hungover
instead of practicing.

844
00:45:23,178 --> 00:45:26,223
Do you know how many people
would kill to get in that boat? I would.

845
00:45:26,724 --> 00:45:30,269
That's cute, but the men are rowing.
Enjoy sweeping.

846
00:45:30,894 --> 00:45:33,272
Huh. Maybe you're onto something.

847
00:45:33,939 --> 00:45:35,149
You want in the boat?

848
00:45:36,108 --> 00:45:39,111
Position's up for grabs. Coxswain.

849
00:45:39,737 --> 00:45:43,449
Liam, Teagan.
You're both going to race for that spot.

850
00:45:43,532 --> 00:45:45,701
Uh, sorry, what?

851
00:45:45,784 --> 00:45:49,413
Okay. Two boats, four rowers, one K.

852
00:45:49,496 --> 00:45:51,331
Liam and Teagan, you each coxswain a boat.

853
00:45:51,415 --> 00:45:53,167
[laughs] I'm not racing her.

854
00:45:53,250 --> 00:45:54,710
Then you're not coxswain.

855
00:45:56,211 --> 00:45:58,130
Losing team
has to clean the docks for a month.

856
00:45:58,881 --> 00:46:01,133
-What?
-Pick your teams. Teagan, you're up.

857
00:46:02,050 --> 00:46:03,802
-Me?
-Come on.

858
00:46:06,764 --> 00:46:11,351
-Cam, Baloo, Josh.
-That's cute, but I'm not rowing for her.

859
00:46:11,435 --> 00:46:12,853
She called your name.

860
00:46:17,065 --> 00:46:18,400
She can take Ryder.

861
00:46:19,067 --> 00:46:22,029
She can have Crabcatcher
and I'll take Noah.

862
00:46:22,613 --> 00:46:24,072
-Fine.
-[Hayden] All right, let's go.

863
00:46:25,157 --> 00:46:27,701
These guys are never going to row for me.

864
00:46:28,410 --> 00:46:31,705
Listen, you're not like
any coxie they had before.

865
00:46:31,789 --> 00:46:33,415
You can pick up on things that they don't.

866
00:46:33,499 --> 00:46:36,376
I don't know how to cox. I'm a rower.

867
00:46:36,460 --> 00:46:39,171
All right, so you know exactly
what it's like to be in their shoes.

868
00:46:39,254 --> 00:46:42,090
Use it. Empathize with them.
Get in their heads.

869
00:46:42,633 --> 00:46:44,468
Listen, this is your chance
to get in the boat.

870
00:46:45,135 --> 00:46:46,136
Do you want it?

871
00:46:46,845 --> 00:46:47,846
Yeah, I do.

872
00:46:47,930 --> 00:46:49,348
Then prove it.

873
00:46:50,974 --> 00:46:51,975
Yeah, okay.

874
00:46:52,059 --> 00:46:53,977
-[indistinct dialog]
-[Teagan clears throat]

875
00:46:55,354 --> 00:46:58,482
I know you don't want to be
on my team, but…

876
00:46:58,565 --> 00:47:02,486
I'm the thing standing in between you
and a month's worth of goose shit. So…

877
00:47:03,987 --> 00:47:05,239
Here's the plan.

878
00:47:06,573 --> 00:47:08,909
The first 250,
we'll let them set the pace.

879
00:47:08,992 --> 00:47:11,912
Liam won't bring them out quick.
He has too much to prove.

880
00:47:12,788 --> 00:47:15,499
When they lag, we'll make our move.

881
00:47:16,166 --> 00:47:17,209
Okay.

882
00:47:17,876 --> 00:47:18,877
[Teagan] Great.

883
00:47:18,961 --> 00:47:20,295
Uh, wait.

884
00:47:21,588 --> 00:47:23,507
I know you only joined to throw the race.

885
00:47:23,590 --> 00:47:24,883
-What, who, me?
-Yeah.

886
00:47:26,802 --> 00:47:28,095
Consider this.

887
00:47:29,680 --> 00:47:32,349
You're only ever gonna be Josh's sidekick.

888
00:47:34,309 --> 00:47:35,310
Piss off.

889
00:47:37,062 --> 00:47:40,399
He'll never consider you as an equal
until you beat him.

890
00:47:43,235 --> 00:47:48,031
["The Best" by Tina Turner playing]

891
00:47:52,703 --> 00:47:57,291
All right. In your ready positions.
We got this.

892
00:47:59,334 --> 00:48:03,755
All right, boys. Let's get this.
Let's show this chick what's up at Easton.

893
00:48:03,839 --> 00:48:06,425
-[horn blows]
-Three-quarter!

894
00:48:06,508 --> 00:48:07,426
[Teagan] Row!

895
00:48:08,427 --> 00:48:11,722
Row. Okay, push. Or legs.

896
00:48:11,805 --> 00:48:14,558
Get off the rate in two. That's one.

897
00:48:15,309 --> 00:48:17,811
That's two. Here we go.
Give it to me, Josh.

898
00:48:17,895 --> 00:48:19,271
Let's go.

899
00:48:21,773 --> 00:48:23,358
And row!

900
00:48:24,067 --> 00:48:26,278
And swing.

901
00:48:26,987 --> 00:48:31,408
And legs. Keep with our plan. Let's go.
Come on. You got this.

902
00:48:32,200 --> 00:48:36,538
And okay, here it is. They're losing it.
Let's take it to them. Come on.

903
00:48:37,080 --> 00:48:38,165
Okay?

904
00:48:38,874 --> 00:48:40,584
Come on. Come on, Ryder.

905
00:48:41,752 --> 00:48:44,171
<i>♪ And it can't be wrong ♪</i>

906
00:48:44,254 --> 00:48:46,340
Okay. You really going to let him win?

907
00:48:46,423 --> 00:48:49,509
<i>♪ Take my heart and make it strong, babe ♪</i>

908
00:48:51,053 --> 00:48:53,388
That's right, Ryder. Let's go. Push!

909
00:48:53,472 --> 00:48:57,935
And legs! Let's go, let's go!

910
00:49:00,479 --> 00:49:02,564
<i>♪ Better than anyone ♪</i>

911
00:49:02,648 --> 00:49:04,691
[Liam] Hey! They're catching up.

912
00:49:05,609 --> 00:49:07,194
We gotta go, we gotta go!

913
00:49:09,446 --> 00:49:12,282
[Teagan] That's right, Ryder.
You got this. Come on!

914
00:49:12,366 --> 00:49:15,577
-And row! Try to bring up pace!
-[Liam] All together! Come on.

915
00:49:15,661 --> 00:49:17,079
They're right on us. Let's go!

916
00:49:17,162 --> 00:49:19,456
Go, go, let's go!

917
00:49:19,539 --> 00:49:20,874
[Teagan] Come on. Five more!

918
00:49:20,958 --> 00:49:25,170
We're losing to a girl!
Can you go a little harder!

919
00:49:25,253 --> 00:49:29,466
And three. Almost there. Two… one!

920
00:49:31,259 --> 00:49:32,511
[horn blows]

921
00:49:32,594 --> 00:49:33,804
Let's go!

922
00:49:35,472 --> 00:49:38,809
Let's go! You guys did it!

923
00:49:38,892 --> 00:49:41,228
You just won! We just won.

924
00:49:41,311 --> 00:49:46,066
Let's go! Teagan! Not bad, crew girl.

925
00:49:46,149 --> 00:49:48,110
Are you freaking kidding me?

926
00:49:51,613 --> 00:49:53,448
Nice job, Ryder.

927
00:49:57,869 --> 00:49:58,829
[exhales]

928
00:50:00,831 --> 00:50:02,040
[Baloo] Hey!

929
00:50:03,083 --> 00:50:05,460
Make my baby spotless.

930
00:50:05,544 --> 00:50:07,754
You guys are goddamn losers.

931
00:50:08,630 --> 00:50:11,425
Just wait.
You'll come crawling back to me.

932
00:50:12,467 --> 00:50:14,720
You know what?
I'm out of here. Who's with me?

933
00:50:16,096 --> 00:50:17,097
Sick.

934
00:50:21,893 --> 00:50:23,729
Hey. Uh…

935
00:50:28,316 --> 00:50:30,610
I just wanted to say sorry for…

936
00:50:32,362 --> 00:50:35,365
lying to you. I'm kind of a mess.

937
00:50:36,491 --> 00:50:38,869
I get it. I also need to focus on crew.

938
00:50:39,369 --> 00:50:41,121
Everything else is a distraction.

939
00:50:48,336 --> 00:50:49,337
Teagan.

940
00:50:51,715 --> 00:50:52,883
You made the team.

941
00:50:53,759 --> 00:50:57,846
So access to the ergs, rowing tanks,
boats. Keep up your training.

942
00:50:59,931 --> 00:51:02,726
What about access to the water
for sculling?

943
00:51:02,809 --> 00:51:05,854
-Or… competing at the regattas?
-Yeah.

944
00:51:05,937 --> 00:51:09,149
Get the boys winning again
and we'll see how far we can push admin.

945
00:51:09,232 --> 00:51:11,068
But remember, eights is a team sport.

946
00:51:11,610 --> 00:51:14,446
The team comes first. Are you ready?

947
00:51:22,079 --> 00:51:24,247
I'm ready. Yeah. [laughing]

948
00:51:24,331 --> 00:51:25,624
All right, boys.

949
00:51:26,291 --> 00:51:28,210
Meet your new coxie, Teagan Tao.

950
00:51:28,293 --> 00:51:33,381
[Baloo] Whoo! Teagan Tao!
Let's go, girl! Up top.

951
00:51:34,132 --> 00:51:37,135
Down below. Split the difference.
Double time.

952
00:51:37,219 --> 00:51:41,389
-Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey! Ah!
-Ow.

953
00:51:41,473 --> 00:51:42,516
Whoo!

954
00:51:43,725 --> 00:51:44,726
What's good?

955
00:51:45,602 --> 00:51:46,853
[Teagan laughs awkwardly]

956
00:51:50,273 --> 00:51:52,275
[stirring music playing]

957
00:51:53,151 --> 00:51:54,069
[Baloo] Mm-hmm.

958
00:51:55,904 --> 00:51:57,155
[Teagan laughs]

959
00:52:10,710 --> 00:52:13,630
[Teagan] <i>A good catch</i>
<i>can send you soaring.</i>

960
00:52:14,589 --> 00:52:19,761
Mom? Guess what? Hello?

961
00:52:26,685 --> 00:52:28,228
That's boring.

962
00:52:29,271 --> 00:52:30,438
Boring.

963
00:52:35,735 --> 00:52:39,698
{\an8}[tense music playing]

964
00:52:39,781 --> 00:52:43,952
{\an8}<i>But one bad catch can end your run.</i>

